{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i 'quiescent|G0|GO_0044838|PATO_0001707|PATO_0002355|PATO_0000586|PATO_0002354|PATO_0001997|dormant|inactive' src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\"","aggregated_output":"3706:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000001 \"Covers cells actively being cultured or stored in a quiescent state for future use.\")\n3718:Covers cells actively being cultured or stored in a quiescent state for future use.\")\n3784:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000010 \"Note that this class was re-labeled to 'cultured cell' instead of 'cell line cell', as it intent was clarified to cover any cultured cells of multicellular and unicellular organisms. This includes cells actively being cultured, or cells that have been cultured but are stored in a quiescent state for future use. In having been cultured, cells must establish homeostasis and often replicate in a foreign environment. Accomodation of this stress initiates a selection of cells fit for such challenges, wherein necessary adaptive biochemical and.or genetic changes can occur. These changes can set them apart from the in vivo cells from which they derive, and such changes will typically accumulate and change over increasing time in culture.\")\n5251:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21907708\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30571046\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Gastric_chief_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000155 \"An epithelial cell of the stomach that is part of the fundic gastric gland. This cell is characterized by a basally located nucleus, abundant rough endoplasmic reticulum, and large apical secretory granules. It produces and secretes pepsinogen, the inactive precursor of the digestive enzyme pepsin.\")\n8554:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0618947256\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000563 \"A rounded, inactive form that certain bacteria assume under conditions of extreme temperature, dryness, or lack of food. The bacterium develops a waterproof cell wall that protects it from being dried out or damaged.\")\n8852:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D032496\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21849021\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000594 \"An elongated, spindle-shaped, cell that is located between the basal lamina and the plasmalemma of a muscle fiber. These cells are mostly quiescent, but upon activation they divide to produce cells that generate new muscle fibers.\")\n15456:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FMA:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002141 \"A parathyroid chief cell that is actively secreting hormone. Have large Golgi complexes with numerous vesicles and small membrane-bound granules; secretory granules are rare, cytoplasmic glycogen sparse, much of the cytoplasm being occupied by flat sacs of granular endoplasmic reticulum in parallel arrays; in normal humans, inactive chief cells outnumber active chief cells in a ratio of 3-5:1\")\n16041:# Class: obo:CL_0002197 (inactive chief cell of parathyoid gland)\n16043:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002197 \"A parathyroid chief cell that is not actively secreting hormone. Contains small Golgi complexes with only a few grouped vesicles and membrane-bound secretory granules; glycogen and many lipofuscin granules abound but sacs of granular endoplasmic reticulum are rare and dispersed. In normal humans, inactive chief cells out number active chief cells in a ratio of 3-5:1.\")\n16046:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002197 \"inactive chief cell of parathyoid gland\")\n16705:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31869123\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002258 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the thyroid follicle epithelium, with a shape that ranges from squamous when inactive to cuboidal or columnar when active, reflecting its hormonal activity. Its apical surface is lined with microvilli projecting into the colloid-filled lumen, where it synthesizes, stores, and secretes the thyroid hormones thyroxine (T4) and triiodothyronine (T3), releasing them into the bloodstream in response to thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH).\")\n17606:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15339667\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20568222\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9520465\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002337 \"A stem cell found in the basal layer of the epidermis, hair follicle, and sebaceous gland, characterised by its quiescent nature, high proliferative potential, and capacity for long-term self-renewal. This cell maintains epidermal homeostasis by producing transit-amplifying cells that differentiate to replenish the stratified squamous epithelium.\")\n17790:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002355 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002417 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000922) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000008467) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000008857) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0000586)))\n17801:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002356 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002417 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0000586) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0002355)))\n18520:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002428 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000809 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0000586) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000056 obo:GO_0008283)))\n19125:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002488 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000351 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0000586) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0001974)))\n20444:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18396103\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002628 \"quiescent microglia\")\n22606:Covers cells actively being cultured or stored in a quiescent state for future use.\")\n22620:Covers cells actively being cultured or stored in a quiescent state for future use.\")\n22774:# Class: obo:CL_0008012 (quiescent skeletal muscle satellite cell)\n22776:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21849021\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23303905\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008012 \"A skeletal muscle satellite cell that is mitotically quiescent.  These cells are wedge shaped and have a large nuclear to cytoplasmic ratio with few organelles, a small nucleus and condensed interphase chromatin. Satellite cells typically remain in this state until activated following muscle damage.\")\n22777:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008012 \"quiescent skeletal muscle satellite cell\")\n32597:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033083 \"Often in literature squamous granulosa cell and pre-granulosa cell are used as synonyms. However, this term only makes reference to the quiescent granulosa cells that surround the primordial ovarian follicle, while a pre-granulosa cell proliferates to form the primordial follicle (and thus cells become the squamous granulosa cells).\")\n33051:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(terms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <doi:10.3389/fendo.2019.00401>) foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042017 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/fendo-10-00401-g001.jpg>)\n33052:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <doi:10.3389/fnins.2022.1129414>) Annotation(rdfs:comment \"α1 tanycytes are the most dorsally located subtype, followed by α2 tanycytes, then β1 tanycytes, and finally β2 tanycytes which occupy the ventricular floor. 3V, third ventricle; Arc, arcuate nucleus; DMH, dorsomedial hypothalamic nucleus; VMH, ventromedial hypothalamic nucleus.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042017 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/fnins-16-1129414-g001.jpg>)\n33065:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(terms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <doi:10.3389/fendo.2019.00401>) foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042018 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/fendo-10-00401-g001.jpg>)\n33066:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <doi:10.3389/fnins.2022.1129414>) Annotation(rdfs:comment \"α1 tanycytes are the most dorsally located subtype, followed by α2 tanycytes, then β1 tanycytes, and finally β2 tanycytes which occupy the ventricular floor. 3V, third ventricle; Arc, arcuate nucleus; DMH, dorsomedial hypothalamic nucleus; VMH, ventromedial hypothalamic nucleus.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042018 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/fnins-16-1129414-g001.jpg>)\n33078:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(terms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <doi:10.3389/fendo.2019.00401>) foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042019 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/fendo-10-00401-g001.jpg>)\n33079:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <doi:10.3389/fnins.2022.1129414>) Annotation(rdfs:comment \"α1 tanycytes are the most dorsally located subtype, followed by α2 tanycytes, then β1 tanycytes, and finally β2 tanycytes which occupy the ventricular floor. 3V, third ventricle; Arc, arcuate nucleus; DMH, dorsomedial hypothalamic nucleus; VMH, ventromedial hypothalamic nucleus.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4042019 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/fnins-16-1129414-g001.jpg>)\n33094:AnnotationA